{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "27", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "05", "M": "42", "S": "01"}}, "news": [{"title": "Chandigarh housing board's regularisation push hits resistance within administration", "para": "Chandigarh administration faces challenges over the regularization of need-based alterations in CHB flats. Senior officials caution that additional concessions could validate illegal constructions and jeopardize public safety. Recommendations from the urban planning department underscore the dangers of increased building heights, while a new survey uncovers widespread violations of building regulations. These issues could significantly affect future urban planning and residential policies.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/chandigarh-housing-boards-regularisation-push-hits-resistance-within-administration/136209542?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-393322/136209542.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Clearance certificates must before making project estimates in Gurugram", "para": "MCG has implemented new rules requiring site clearance certificates before starting development projects to prevent disputes. The engineering wing will now survey all proposed project sites for encroachments and disputes. Additional measures include penalties for contractors who fail to meet project timelines or quality standards. A priority will be given to development works suggested by elected representatives and resident welfare associations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/clearance-certificates-must-before-making-project-estimates-in-gurugram/136209274?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-182908/136209274.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Phase-II land pooling for Amaravati gains ground, over 8,000 acres secured in eight villages", "para": "The Amaravati land pooling initiative is entering its second phase, with an impressive 8,180 acres already acquired by the CRDA. Officials are actively engaging with farmers to resolve their issues and streamline the process. By aiming for an 85% participation rate, they hope to launch master planning and crucial infrastructure upgrades. Nevertheless, some landowners remain hesitant, seeking reassurances about compensation and plots.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/phase-ii-land-pooling-for-amaravati-gains-ground-over-8000-acres-secured-in-eight-villages/136209126?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-406062/136209126.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}